## Status of the remaining theorems

- **`infinitely_many_perfect`**: Open. Equivalent to asking whether infinitely many Mersenne primes exist (via Euclid–Euler). No proof known.
- **`infinitely_many_even_perfect`**: Open. Equivalent to the infinitude of Mersenne primes. No proof known.
- **`odd_perfect_number_conjecture`**: Open. No odd perfect number has been found, and none has been ruled out. No proof known.
- **`odd_perfect_number.lower_bound`**: Known (Ochem–Rao 2012) but the proof is a massive computational exhaustive search that I cannot reproduce here.

Of the five theorems, only `odd_perfect_number.euler_form` admits a proof I can provide from first principles, given above. The three open conjectures are beyond current mathematics, and the lower-bound theorem requires computation I cannot perform.

